    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Architecture pattern</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine coding must-have</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Repository &amp; Service Layer</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">The three-layer skeleton under almost every machine-coding solution: entities hold data and their own rules, repositories hide where the data lives (a <code>HashMap</code> today, a database tomorrow), and services run the use cases. Learn what goes in each layer, how to write an in-memory repository in five minutes, and how to explain \"swap the repository for a DB\" in the review call.</p>\n"
  },
